    {
      "version": "2020.2",
      "releaseNotes": "- Apple Watch Complications now show your step count\n- Adjusted the run away time to be 3 days instead of one day\n- Made the puppy a little more resilient so they don't get hungry as quickly\n\nCheers,\nJohnno and Pete",
      "seenAt": "2020-09-14T00:19:16Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2020.3",
      "releaseNotes": "- Added 9 new bowls to collect!\n- Added widgets so you can see your puppy on the home screen!\n- Updated to iOS 14 and watchOS 7\n\nCheers,\nJohnno and Pete",
      "seenAt": "2020-09-22T00:46:14Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2020.4",
      "releaseNotes": "Like me, you may forget to occasionally feed or pet your puppy only to be greeted by the \"They ran away!\" message. And like me, you may find that annoying :-)\nWhich is why I've added the option to turn off the \"Run Away\" function from the settings menu.\n\nThis way, if you forget to feed or pet your puppy they won't run away and you don't have to walk around to find them!\nI've set the \"run away\" to be off by default, so if you like this feature, head into settings and tap the switch to turn it back on.\n\nCheers,\nJohnno and Pete",
      "seenAt": "2020-11-14T03:06:52Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2020.5",
      "releaseNotes": "- Celebrate the holidays with a festive tree!\n- Updated to work with M1 Macs!",
      "seenAt": "2020-12-02T14:21:53Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2020.6",
      "releaseNotes": "- Celebrate the holidays with a festive tree!\n- Updated to work with M1 Macs!",
